-- title:
--   Geometric function field of X₀(ℓ) as ℚ̄(j)(j_ℓ)
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a prime. Write $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ for `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` and work inside the Laurent series field $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ (`LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`). On one side stands `modularFunctionFieldBar ℓ`, by definition the base change `laurentBaseChange` of `modularFunctionFieldFull ℓ`: that is, the intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise embedding `coeffEmb` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ into $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull ℓ`, itself the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ the set `divisorExpansions ℓ`. On the other side stands the two-step simple adjunction: first adjoin to $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ the series `jqModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, namely $q^{-1}$ times the image in $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}[[q]]$ of the integral power series `jNum` $= E_4^3 \cdot$ `dedekindEtaUnitInv`, and then adjoin to that field the series `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) ℓ`, the image of `jqModC` under the substitution $q \mapsto q^{\ell}$ given by `qExpand`. The assertion is that the two intermediate fields coincide, the second being read as an intermediate field over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ via `IntermediateField.restrictScalars`.
--
--   This identifies the geometric function field of $X_0(\ell)$ with $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}(j)(j_\ell)$, where $j$ and $j_\ell$ are the $q$-expansions of $j(z)$ and $j(\ell z)$, thereby connecting the base-changed modular function field with the tower $\bar{\mathbb{Q}} \subseteq \bar{\mathbb{Q}}(j) \subseteq \bar{\mathbb{Q}}(j, j_\ell)$ in which degrees and modular polynomials are available. It is used when producing places of the function field from roots of the modular polynomial and in the computation of the relative rank of `laurentBaseChange`.
-- source:
